# Components: base on bits-ui

Before building interactive UI (buttons, dialogs, menus, selects, tabs, etc.), check [bits-ui](https://bits-ui.com) for an existing primitive. Wrap that primitive in our `$lib/components/ui` layer — do not reimplement accessibility, focus, or keyboard behavior from scratch.

## Patterns

- Import the bits-ui primitive (e.g. `Button as ButtonPrimitive`).
- Extend primitive props (`ButtonPrimitive.RootProps`) and add our variants/sizes.
- Use Svelte 5 runes (`$props`, `$derived`, snippets).
- Put shared UI under `src/lib/components/ui/<name>/` with `index.ts` re-exports.
- Style with Tailwind + [tailwind-variants](https://www.tailwind-variants.org/) recipes (`*.styles.ts`); keep behavior in bits-ui.

```svelte
<!-- ✅ GOOD — wrap bits-ui + tv recipe -->
<script lang="ts">
	import { Button as ButtonPrimitive } from 'bits-ui';
	import type { Snippet } from 'svelte';
	import type { ButtonVariantProps } from './button.styles.js';
	import { buttonVariants } from './button.styles.js';

	type Props = ButtonPrimitive.RootProps & ButtonVariantProps & { children?: Snippet };

	const { variant = 'primary', size = 'md', class: className, children, ...restProps }: Props =
		$props();

	const slots = $derived(buttonVariants({ variant, size }));
</script>

<ButtonPrimitive.Root {...restProps} class={slots.base({ class: className })}>
	{@render children?.()}
</ButtonPrimitive.Root>
```

## Do not

- Build custom click/focus/escape handling when bits-ui already provides it
- Use a different headless UI library for the same role
- Put one-off styled primitives only in a route — prefer `components/ui` when reusable
